  "_doc": "THE DECK. One entry per page — this is the part a human writes. Nothing here is in seconds: atBar is a BAR NUMBER on the measured grid (data/features.json), and every entrance is measured in BEATS from the page turn. A page turn is a cut on the grid.\nMark ONE block per page as `hit` — the moment the page is about; the lens reacts to it. Two hits in six pages is the target; a hit on a third of the pages is not a hit.\nThe last page demonstrates MV mode: layout \"stage\", a full-bleed `scene` motif and one `lyric` line, with no page number and no progress bar — those are lecture-deck furniture.\nAll copy in this example is about the method itself. It quotes no song, no lyrics, and no third-party artwork, so the example can ship with the skill.",
